Charles Wiggins Cobb was an American mathematician and economist and a 1912 Ph.D graduate. 
He published many works on both subjects. 
Charles Cobb and Paul Douglas published a study in which they modeled the growth of the american economey during the period 1899-1922. 
They considered the simplified view of the economy in which production of output is determined by the amount of labor involved and the amount of capital used. 
While there are many other factors affecting economic performance, their model proved to be be remarkably accurate. 
